#
# reconstruct_fallible_operations: rewrite the uses of a checked operation's result in every block
#
# The rewrite of 'r := x checked.+ y; assert(!r.1)' into 'r := x panic.+ y' changes
# the type of r to the integer type, but replaced the uses of r.0 only in the same
# block. A use after a call terminator (e.g. 'v[i] = a + b', whose place
# IndexMut::index_mut(&mut v, i) is computed after the sum) kept 'move r.0' with
# r: usize, an ill-typed LLBC (Aeneas: expand_symbolic_value_no_branching on a
# TLiteral). The use counts are now taken over the whole body, the rewrite is
# skipped unless the tuple is only used through r.0 (and the asserted r.1), and
# the r.0 uses of every rewritten tuple are replaced body-wide.

